# Graphify knowledge-graph output. A derived artifact — rebuildable with `graphify update .`
graphify-out/

# M6 — the live-Nextcloud test suite's connection details, including an app password.
# SPEC §13.2 requires the merge matrix to run against a real server, and a real server
# needs a real credential. The suite reads env vars first and this file second, so CI
# never needs the file to exist; a developer's copy must never be committed.
nextcloud-test.local.properties

# ⚠️ Every `*.local.properties`, by pattern rather than by name. The two above were listed
# individually, which works right up until somebody adds a third — and M12's third one holds a
# live AssemblyAI key that bills a real card. A credential file that is ignored only if someone
# remembered to list it is a credential file that gets committed.
*.local.properties

# M7's accuracy corpus. IAMonDo v1.0 is licensed for NON-COMMERCIAL RESEARCH USE and confers no
# redistribution right, so it must never be committed — only the aggregate numbers, which live in
# docs/M7-RECOGNITION.md. `tools/m7-accuracy.ps1` fetches it into a scratch directory outside the
# working tree; these patterns are the belt to that braces, for anyone who unpacks it here.
IAMonDo-db-1.0/
IAMonDo-db-1.0.tar.gz

# Python bytecode from tools/m7.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ⚠️ M12 — recorded lectures. NEVER commit these.
#
# A recording is a classroom: a teacher and other students, very likely minors, none of whom
# agreed to be in a git history. It is also the one file this app holds that cannot be re-made,
# so a commit is not just a privacy problem but a permanent one — git keeps it after a delete.
# `tools/pull-recordings.ps1` defaults to `recordings-pulled/`, which is one `git add .` away
# from exactly that.
#
# The transcript is the same data in a form that is easier to read and easier to search, so it
# is listed too.
recordings-pulled/
*.opus
*.timeline

# Unpacked AAR contents from reading androidx.ink with `javap` — the only way to settle what is
# `@RestrictTo` and what a package is really called (see CLAUDE.md's notes on M1, M4 and M7).
# Scratch, reproducible from the Gradle cache, and 4.8 MB of it.
/nl/
/strokes/

# Python bytecode from the M12 tools.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# A stray file my own shell quoting kept creating. Belt and braces.
$LOG
